WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:07.090
- [Man] I think you
should never be scared.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.342
(cheering)

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.848
(shouting and chanting)

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.981
Even if China stronger,

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:24.899
China will give you only good.

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:27.777
- You can talk here, not like China.

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:29.070
A dictatorship.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.281
A fascist dictatorship.

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:32.657
- This is my book.

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:35.952
This is called in Chinese
(speaks in Chinese).

00:00:35.952 --> 00:00:38.121
English, American Economy.

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:41.750
- We fail to appreciate history.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.168
We fail to think,

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:47.797
and it's cost us fiercely, in that today

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:50.884
the United States is in deep decline.

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:54.304
- The problem with GM

00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:58.475
is not caused by Toyota or Hyundai either.

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:02.479
The problem with General
Motors has been caused by what?

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:04.439
General Motors and the UAW.

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:05.482
- We're not very competitive.

00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:08.067
We've been spending too
much money on making,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.904
ultimately, worthless stuff.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.281
- You are making weapons,
you are making tanks

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:14.574
to kill people, okay?

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:18.578
China is actually making
cups, utensils, cloths.

00:01:19.787 --> 00:01:21.706
- We gave a lot of people

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:24.542
in a lot of labs and factories and things

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:28.588
good jobs to make plutonium
weapons, uranium weapons,

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.090
things of this sort,
for all of these years,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.593
and it didn't contribute one iota

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.930
to either consumption or
investment in America.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.265
It was technical waste.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:42.227
And we're now paying the costs for it.

00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:45.230
(speaks in Chinese)

00:01:50.818 --> 00:01:54.322
Our economics has been
revealed for some time

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:56.199
as being ideological,

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:58.534
as ideological as Marxism/Leninism

00:01:58.534 --> 00:01:59.702
ever ever thought it would be.

00:01:59.702 --> 00:02:01.704
We take a book and say it's in here,

00:02:01.704 --> 00:02:05.875
and this is the revealed
truth whether it works or not.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.634
(speaks in Chinese)

00:02:17.053 --> 00:02:20.223
- (laughs) Different.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.685
China is a very promising country.

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:27.605
I'm sure, in 20 years,
we'll catch up with USA.

00:03:02.724 --> 00:03:07.353
- The world hegemon has
historically always been

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.856
the world's most powerful economic nation.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.232
The United States hasn't been

00:03:11.232 --> 00:03:15.403
the most powerful economic
nation for a long time now.

00:03:19.073 --> 00:03:22.910
And it doesn't look like
it's gonna come back.

00:03:31.919 --> 00:03:33.838
- [Narrator] The decline
of the United States

00:03:33.838 --> 00:03:37.133
as the world hegemon is
a necessary condition

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:40.553
in order for China to take over that role

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:48.978
But does hegemon necessarily mean empire?

00:03:48.978 --> 00:03:52.190
- Hegemon simply refers
to an overarching power.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.818
By empire, then, I think it's
a little bit like pornography,

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:58.070
you'll know it when you see it.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.991
As China unleashes its tremendous talents,

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:05.077
as well as the power of
its size and productivity,

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:09.081
it certainly is assuming
a hegemonic position.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.583
But, I don't think China

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.669
quite qualifies as an empire right now.

00:04:13.669 --> 00:04:14.837
- [Narrator] But, historically,

00:04:14.837 --> 00:04:16.756
when countries have become hegemons,

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:19.342
they eventually become empires.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:21.844
Rome.

00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:29.477
(shouting and clashing of swords)

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.604
Britain.

00:04:35.316 --> 00:04:39.070
(woman sobs and child cries)

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:41.447
Germany.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.537
(cheering)

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.624
Japan.

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.630
(guns fire)

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.467
Russia.

00:05:11.435 --> 00:05:14.855
And, let's not forget, the United States.

00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:24.448
(shouting and clanging of steel)

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:32.623
(explosions boom)

00:05:46.137 --> 00:05:48.347
- The Americans don't realize,

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:52.518
we have probably a good thousand
overseas military bases.

00:05:53.936 --> 00:05:54.895
- [Narrator] China doesn't yet have

00:05:54.895 --> 00:05:57.481
this military capability.

00:05:57.481 --> 00:05:58.899
But, what happens when it becomes

00:05:58.899 --> 00:06:01.527
the world's number one economy?

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:05.531
Will hegemony lead it to
become the world's next empire?

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.450
Or, does it provide a much needed balance

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.535
to American militarism?

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.787
(shouting)

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.540
Should we be afraid?

00:06:19.587 --> 00:06:21.464
- Seeing is believing.

00:06:21.464 --> 00:06:24.008
So, come to China and have a look.

00:06:24.008 --> 00:06:25.342
- [Narrator] Seeing is believing.

00:06:25.342 --> 00:06:26.635
So, let's go.

00:06:26.635 --> 00:06:28.888
But, not only to China.

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.307
Lets go to the countries
that surround China

00:06:31.307 --> 00:06:34.769
and see how they're being treated.

00:06:34.769 --> 00:06:38.022
Is China being a friendly neighbor?

00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:40.191
Or, is it sowing the seeds

00:06:41.942 --> 00:06:42.777
of empire.

00:06:51.994 --> 00:06:54.038
China already uses its neighbors

00:06:54.038 --> 00:06:56.457
to play big country politics.

00:06:58.167 --> 00:06:59.752
Busan, South Korea.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.172
One of the word's major shipping ports

00:07:03.172 --> 00:07:04.381
and evidence of the

00:07:04.381 --> 00:07:07.301
successful industrialization
of South Korea,

00:07:07.301 --> 00:07:11.889
who's living standards now rival
those of the United States.

00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:15.935
The US considers South Korea
a key ally in East Asia,

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:18.354
and it hopes that China
will help to resolve

00:07:18.354 --> 00:07:20.064
the growing nuclear threat

00:07:20.064 --> 00:07:23.150
posed by neighboring North Korea.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:27.321
Like much US policy, it
misunderstands Chinese interests.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.659
(folk music)

00:07:45.673 --> 00:07:49.009
Korea used to be a tributary,
or satellite state,

00:07:49.009 --> 00:07:51.554
of the historical Chinese empire.

00:07:51.554 --> 00:07:55.683
At one point even referring
to itself as Sojunghwa,

00:07:55.683 --> 00:07:57.017
or Little China.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:02.231
It was split in two during the
1950-1953 Korean Civil War,

00:08:06.735 --> 00:08:09.196
with the reclusive communist North

00:08:09.196 --> 00:08:12.283
allying itself with Russia and China.

00:08:13.909 --> 00:08:17.246
Meanwhile, the South chose
developmental capitalism,

00:08:17.246 --> 00:08:19.665
and relied heavily on
the vast consumer markets

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.584
of the United States

00:08:21.584 --> 00:08:24.128
to propel its rabid industrialization

00:08:24.128 --> 00:08:26.547
through export driven growth.

00:08:28.215 --> 00:08:30.843
Seoul, the nation's capital,

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:33.804
has a little more than a quarter
of the county's population

00:08:33.804 --> 00:08:34.972
of 48 million.

00:08:36.724 --> 00:08:39.310
It sits precariously at 50 kilometers

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:43.314
from the demilitarized zone
separating the two sides,

00:08:43.314 --> 00:08:46.150
in range of the North's artillery.

00:08:48.068 --> 00:08:50.070
Threat of Seoul's all out destruction

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:51.905
in the event of further conflict

00:08:51.905 --> 00:08:56.076
has helped maintain this
status quo for five decades.

00:08:59.913 --> 00:09:01.165
Just how serious a threat

00:09:01.165 --> 00:09:05.169
is North Korea's development
of nuclear weapons?

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:11.342
(thunderous explosion)

00:09:19.433 --> 00:09:20.476
- In order for a country

00:09:20.476 --> 00:09:24.438
to become a full-fledged
nuclear weapons state,

00:09:24.438 --> 00:09:27.524
the country should
satisfy four conditions.

00:09:27.524 --> 00:09:31.403
The first condition is
production of nuclear warhead.

00:09:31.403 --> 00:09:34.823
Yes, North Korea has
acquired nuclear warhead.

00:09:34.823 --> 00:09:38.368
Second, they should have
delivery capability.

00:09:38.368 --> 00:09:40.287
North Korea has delivery capability.

00:09:40.287 --> 00:09:43.415
It has intermediate
range ballistic missile,

00:09:43.415 --> 00:09:45.084
Northern One and Northern Two.

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:48.837
It has short range missiles
such as SCUD B and C.

00:09:48.837 --> 00:09:51.173
Third, nuclear testing.

00:09:51.173 --> 00:09:55.010
But, there's a debate on whether
it was successful or not.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:58.680
And, finally, in order
to mount the warhead

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.600
on the short and medium range missiles,

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:05.771
North Korea should possess
miniaturization technology.

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:08.774
But, we believe North
Korea is short of acquiring

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:11.276
the miniaturization technology.

00:10:11.276 --> 00:10:12.277
In view of that,

00:10:12.277 --> 00:10:15.447
we can argue that North Korea
is a very dangerous country

00:10:15.447 --> 00:10:18.992
with potential nuclear weapons capability,

00:10:18.992 --> 00:10:21.870
but we cannot regard
North Korea as defacto,

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.873
a full-fledged nuclear weapons state.

00:10:24.873 --> 00:10:28.085
- I don't find the Korean
situation unstable.

00:10:28.085 --> 00:10:32.673
I've never felt that there
was a threat from North Korea.

00:10:32.673 --> 00:10:34.550
I've never thought for a minute

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:36.510
there was a single North Korean

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:39.972
that was even slightly suicidal.

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:42.224
(chanting)

00:10:53.318 --> 00:10:54.653
- [Narrator] Suicidal or not,

00:10:54.653 --> 00:10:58.949
a nuclear North shifts the
balance of power in Asia.

00:10:58.949 --> 00:11:01.076
Why doesn't China use its growing strength

00:11:01.076 --> 00:11:05.372
to help US backed efforts
to disarm North Korea?

00:11:05.372 --> 00:11:07.666
- One of the odd things
about the post war world

00:11:07.666 --> 00:11:10.168
is the Chinese are absolutely delighted

00:11:10.168 --> 00:11:12.671
to have Korea divided in two.

00:11:12.671 --> 00:11:14.506
They used to try and maintain this

00:11:14.506 --> 00:11:16.425
even back in the Tang Dynasty.

00:11:16.425 --> 00:11:20.470
Korea was often structurally
divided into different kingdoms

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.472
with different support from the Chinese,

00:11:22.472 --> 00:11:26.476
because it led to structural weakness,

00:11:26.476 --> 00:11:30.147
inability to stand up
to Chinese domination.

00:11:31.064 --> 00:11:34.026
Their policy is to prevent war

00:11:34.026 --> 00:11:36.737
and prevent the unification of Korea.

00:11:36.737 --> 00:11:40.490
(speaks in foreign language)

00:11:56.923 --> 00:11:58.884
- Initially, when, let's say,

00:11:58.884 --> 00:12:02.137
go back to January and February 2003,

00:12:02.137 --> 00:12:06.099
what the Bush administration wanted was

00:12:06.099 --> 00:12:09.811
press China in such a way that China would

00:12:09.811 --> 00:12:12.481
impose sanctions on North Korea.

00:12:13.648 --> 00:12:15.150
China didn't want it.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.652
- If you're gonna work
on Korean nuclear issues,

00:12:17.652 --> 00:12:20.405
you have to understand the Chinese context

00:12:20.405 --> 00:12:23.909
and the fact that South
Korea is rich is fine,

00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:26.370
but if Korea were unified and this rich,

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.580
it would be the size
of former West Germany.

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:32.751
That's getting to be a little
too big for Chinese comfort.

00:12:37.756 --> 00:12:40.467
- [Narrator] If Korea is a
traditional tributary state

00:12:40.467 --> 00:12:43.136
that China manages through division,

00:12:43.136 --> 00:12:45.389
then how will it deal with Korea's bigger

00:12:45.389 --> 00:12:47.808
and wealthier neighbor Japan,

00:12:48.892 --> 00:12:53.063
who's rivalries with China
have spanned centuries?

00:12:54.606 --> 00:12:55.482
The answer depends,

00:12:55.482 --> 00:12:58.819
not only on the intentions
of the Chinese government,

00:12:58.819 --> 00:13:02.989
but, also, on the attitudes
of the Chinese people.

00:13:03.824 --> 00:13:06.034
Like Korea, Japan has traditionally

00:13:06.034 --> 00:13:09.454
been a part of the Chinese cultural area.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:14.000
But, it has also been fiercely rebellious.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:17.796
After Japan became the first
Asian nation to industrialize,

00:13:17.796 --> 00:13:21.216
it used its newfound strength
to create a modern empire

00:13:21.216 --> 00:13:24.052
and subjugate its Asian neighbors.

00:13:33.812 --> 00:13:35.480
Committing heinous war crimes

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:38.567
and killing approximately
30 million Chinese

00:13:38.567 --> 00:13:39.901
throughout Asia,

00:13:42.362 --> 00:13:44.906
understandably, there
exists a strong current

00:13:44.906 --> 00:13:49.077
of anti-Japanese sentiment
among many Chinese today.

00:13:51.079 --> 00:13:53.999
Although Japan was
defeated in World War Two,

00:13:53.999 --> 00:13:58.169
it went on to become the
world's second largest economy.

00:13:59.421 --> 00:14:00.463
China, however,

00:14:00.463 --> 00:14:04.467
is now on the verge of
surpassing its old rival.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:16.563
To many, both inside China and out,

00:14:16.563 --> 00:14:20.734
the 2008 Beijing Olympics were
a symbol of China's rebirth

00:14:21.818 --> 00:14:24.070
as Asia's preeminent power.

00:14:26.823 --> 00:14:29.492
As part of the Beijing
Olympic torch relay,

00:14:29.492 --> 00:14:33.204
the Chinese decided to bring
the torch to Nagano, Japan,

00:14:33.204 --> 00:14:36.124
home of the 1998 Japanese Olympics,

00:14:37.125 --> 00:14:40.712
perhaps as a message to the
world that the Middle Kingdom

00:14:40.712 --> 00:14:44.716
was about to eclipse the
land of the rising sun.

00:14:45.717 --> 00:14:47.093
Along with this message

00:14:47.093 --> 00:14:50.430
came a tremendous display of nationalism

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:55.143
in the form of thousands of young Chinese.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.438
Many received encouragement

00:14:58.438 --> 00:15:01.900
and even financial support
for their travels to Nagano

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:06.112
from various Chinese
consulates throughout Japan.

00:15:06.112 --> 00:15:07.822
(rock music)

00:15:07.822 --> 00:15:11.159
(cheering and chanting)

00:15:52.909 --> 00:15:54.369
The Chinese government requested

00:15:54.369 --> 00:15:57.372
that the relay began at Zhenguo Ji Temple,

00:15:57.372 --> 00:16:01.543
the same starting point as
that of Japan's 1998 Olympics.

00:16:03.044 --> 00:16:04.212
- Actually, the Olympics games

00:16:04.212 --> 00:16:07.465
is a very good opportunity for China.

00:16:07.465 --> 00:16:10.885
Most of the students in China view it

00:16:10.885 --> 00:16:15.056
as a great opportunity for
us to present ourselves.

00:16:18.685 --> 00:16:21.354
- [Narrator] However,
days before the torch run,

00:16:21.354 --> 00:16:23.398
the temple announced
concerns about the treatment

00:16:23.398 --> 00:16:27.402
of fellow Buddhists in Tibet
at the hands of the Chinese

00:16:27.402 --> 00:16:31.364
and refused to host the Chinese torch.

00:16:31.364 --> 00:16:34.617
(shouting in Japanese)

00:16:59.601 --> 00:17:00.435
The event attracted

00:17:00.435 --> 00:17:03.771
a large number of loosely
associated protestors,

00:17:03.771 --> 00:17:05.148
who took the torch relay

00:17:05.148 --> 00:17:09.319
as an opportunity to voice
grievances against China.

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:18.036
- Generally, we don't like the protestors,

00:17:18.036 --> 00:17:22.457
because they try to insert
political implications

00:17:22.457 --> 00:17:24.459
to this non-political event.

00:17:24.459 --> 00:17:26.544
- [Interviewer] What do you
think about the new railroad

00:17:26.544 --> 00:17:28.046
that goes to Wason?

00:17:28.046 --> 00:17:29.631
- Railroad is good.

00:17:30.965 --> 00:17:34.135
However, most importantly, how to use.

00:17:35.845 --> 00:17:36.679
So...

00:17:38.514 --> 00:17:42.352
So, that should be used for Tibet people,

00:17:42.352 --> 00:17:45.939
not for Chinese.
(shouting)

00:17:52.528 --> 00:17:55.114
- [Interviewer] They are supporting you.

00:17:55.114 --> 00:17:55.949
- Maybe?

00:17:57.742 --> 00:18:01.496
(speaks in foreign language)

00:18:08.252 --> 00:18:11.422
They don't know who is right.

00:18:11.422 --> 00:18:13.675
(shouting)

00:18:16.177 --> 00:18:18.012
- I understand that the protestors,

00:18:18.012 --> 00:18:20.098
they need to get attention of the world.

00:18:20.098 --> 00:18:23.059
But, I don't think
Olympics is a good timing,

00:18:23.059 --> 00:18:27.230
because Olympic is a proud of
everyone of Chinese peoples,

00:18:28.648 --> 00:18:33.611
so, if you protest it, you are
opposing the Chinese people.

00:18:33.611 --> 00:18:36.948
(shouting and cheering)

00:18:56.884 --> 00:18:59.804
- [Narrator] Beyond being a
window on Chinese nationalism,

00:18:59.804 --> 00:19:01.347
the Nagano torch relay

00:19:01.347 --> 00:19:03.266
provided a glimpse into the situation

00:19:03.266 --> 00:19:06.394
of some of China's
various ethnic minorities,

00:19:06.394 --> 00:19:08.563
and begged the question,

00:19:08.563 --> 00:19:11.774
is China really the
unified multi-ethnic nation

00:19:11.774 --> 00:19:13.192
that it portrays?

00:19:33.796 --> 00:19:36.799
- In China's idea, from
ancient to until now,

00:19:36.799 --> 00:19:38.551
we stress harmonious.

00:19:39.552 --> 00:19:41.721
(laughs) Harmonious.

00:19:41.721 --> 00:19:43.473
You know, Confucius.

00:19:43.473 --> 00:19:44.307
Confucius.

00:19:45.266 --> 00:19:48.102
Yeah, from his period 2,000 years ago,

00:19:48.102 --> 00:19:50.104
he teach us be friendly.

00:19:52.732 --> 00:19:56.277
No matter where you come
from, all corner of the world,

00:19:56.277 --> 00:19:57.778
we are one family.

00:19:58.738 --> 00:20:00.698
We are friends.

00:20:00.698 --> 00:20:02.783
- [Narrator] The Olympics
provided an opportunity

00:20:02.783 --> 00:20:06.245
to see if the harmonious
society was a reality

00:20:06.245 --> 00:20:07.997
or simply propaganda.

00:20:10.917 --> 00:20:14.003
We headed to Xinjiang,
meaning new territory,

00:20:14.003 --> 00:20:17.757
to watch the Olympic
torch replay in Kashkar.

00:20:31.354 --> 00:20:33.231
Inside Kashkar City,

00:20:33.231 --> 00:20:37.151
preparations for the
torch relay were underway.

00:20:38.277 --> 00:20:41.239
In a show of ethnic
solidarity for the Olympics,

00:20:41.239 --> 00:20:42.406
the authorities were preparing

00:20:42.406 --> 00:20:46.244
a large group of minority
children, mostly Uyghurs,

00:20:46.244 --> 00:20:48.579
to come out and show support for the torch

00:20:48.579 --> 00:20:50.414
on the day of the run.

00:20:58.047 --> 00:21:02.218
The event itself, however, was
sealed off from the public.

00:21:12.478 --> 00:21:15.064
(ethnic music)

00:21:19.485 --> 00:21:23.114
(sings in foreign language)

00:21:26.826 --> 00:21:28.244
We were struck by just how different

00:21:28.244 --> 00:21:30.913
Xinjiang was from Eastern China,

00:21:31.789 --> 00:21:33.666
and we wanted to know more.

00:21:33.666 --> 00:21:37.003
Specifically, just who were the Uyghurs.

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:40.756
Well, to become with,

00:21:40.756 --> 00:21:43.259
they're Central Asians of Turkic origin,

00:21:43.259 --> 00:21:44.844
and they're Muslim.

00:21:49.265 --> 00:21:50.725
Like other Muslim cultures,

00:21:50.725 --> 00:21:54.645
the Uyghurs treat guests
with the utmost hospitality,

00:21:54.645 --> 00:21:56.772
and we were invited by
a man off the street

00:21:56.772 --> 00:21:59.191
to share tea with his family.

00:22:01.193 --> 00:22:03.320
Like many of the minorities we met,

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:07.241
he asked that we obscure
his face and voice.

00:22:07.241 --> 00:22:10.995
(speaks in foreign language)

00:22:58.459 --> 00:22:59.752
- [Interviewer] Can we ask him

00:22:59.752 --> 00:23:02.254
what he thinks about Iraq war?

00:23:03.506 --> 00:23:07.259
(speaks in foreign language)

00:23:12.139 --> 00:23:15.184
- [Narrator] Afterwards, we
spoke to another Uyghur farmer

00:23:15.184 --> 00:23:16.435
and his family.

00:23:18.771 --> 00:23:22.525
(speaks in foreign language)

00:23:41.961 --> 00:23:43.629
- [Interviewer] What was that?

00:23:43.629 --> 00:23:44.964
What did he say?

00:23:45.881 --> 00:23:48.509
- [Guide] He's saying about
the little situations,

00:23:48.509 --> 00:23:53.347
about that cement factory,
Kashkar Cement Factory,

00:23:53.347 --> 00:23:56.267
about a little bad for the farming.

00:23:59.061 --> 00:24:02.481
- [Interviewer] Yeah, cement factories...

00:24:03.983 --> 00:24:06.652
- [Narrator] We knew we
hadn't gotten the whole story,

00:24:06.652 --> 00:24:09.154
but our guide wouldn't
give us any more details

00:24:09.154 --> 00:24:10.990
on what had been said.

00:24:13.534 --> 00:24:14.994
Although Uyghurs are, by far,

00:24:14.994 --> 00:24:17.788
the largest ethnic group in Xinjiang,

00:24:17.788 --> 00:24:21.417
there are a number of smaller ones.

00:24:21.417 --> 00:24:25.129
We spoke to a Uyghur speaking
ethnic Tajik at his home.

00:24:25.129 --> 00:24:28.841
(speaks in foreign language)

00:24:31.093 --> 00:24:35.264
- He's happy about the
Communistic party of China.

00:24:35.264 --> 00:24:36.098
- Oh, really?

00:24:36.098 --> 00:24:37.307
- Yeah.

00:24:37.307 --> 00:24:41.061
(speaks in foreign language)

00:24:44.648 --> 00:24:48.819
In the past, they make a fire
in the oven in the house.

00:24:49.695 --> 00:24:53.615
All of the inside of the house is smoke.

00:24:53.615 --> 00:24:55.701
Very bad environment.

00:24:55.701 --> 00:24:57.786
But now, not like that.

00:24:57.786 --> 00:24:59.038
- Because he has a new house?

00:24:59.038 --> 00:24:59.872
- Yes.

00:25:02.249 --> 00:25:06.420
- So what is the relationship
to the Communist Party?

00:25:09.256 --> 00:25:13.010
(speaks in foreign language)

00:25:19.349 --> 00:25:23.520
- Oh, they are very, very
satisfied with the party.

00:25:25.355 --> 00:25:29.526
He said never be able to
find another party like this.

00:25:32.571 --> 00:25:33.822
- [Narrator] It wasn't
until we caught up with

00:25:33.822 --> 00:25:36.950
exiled Uyghur spokeswoman Rebiya Kadeer

00:25:36.950 --> 00:25:40.829
at the Uyghur American
Association in Washington, DC,

00:25:40.829 --> 00:25:44.082
that we felt like we got
the other side of the story.

00:25:44.082 --> 00:25:47.836
(speaks in foreign language)

00:26:50.691 --> 00:26:53.944
- Do many Tajiks here go to Tajikistan?

00:26:55.279 --> 00:26:59.032
(speaks in foreign language)

00:27:01.535 --> 00:27:02.953
- No, they don't.

00:27:03.829 --> 00:27:07.124
They don't have the permission
to go to Tajikistan,

00:27:07.124 --> 00:27:09.334
because Tajikistan is another country.

00:27:09.334 --> 00:27:12.296
That this is the small country,

00:27:12.296 --> 00:27:15.716
so, they have no permission to go abroad.

00:27:17.009 --> 00:27:20.012
Some relatives of him in Tajikistan,

00:27:22.264 --> 00:27:26.018
they'll be able to visit
him, but he doesn't.

00:27:26.893 --> 00:27:30.647
(speaks in foreign language)

00:27:39.698 --> 00:27:44.202
- A harmonious society
should be a society that

00:27:44.202 --> 00:27:47.497
balance the interest of
different groups of people,

00:27:47.497 --> 00:27:50.333
for example, the wealthy and the poor,

00:27:50.333 --> 00:27:53.253
the majority and minority people,

00:27:53.253 --> 00:27:56.089
the urban and rural residents,

00:27:56.089 --> 00:27:59.092
and, also, it should be balanced between

00:27:59.092 --> 00:28:01.053
people and the environment.

00:28:01.053 --> 00:28:03.680
- [Narrator] We asked the
Uyghur American Assassination

00:28:03.680 --> 00:28:05.432
to provide a re-translation

00:28:05.432 --> 00:28:08.518
of the Kashkar Cement Factory clip.

00:28:08.518 --> 00:28:09.895
- This old Uyghur farmer

00:28:09.895 --> 00:28:12.481
is complaining about the cement factory

00:28:12.481 --> 00:28:14.649
right across his farmland,

00:28:15.525 --> 00:28:17.652
because the cement factory,

00:28:17.652 --> 00:28:21.073
which is rebuilt, it's modernized,

00:28:21.073 --> 00:28:23.116
and it's polluting the air,

00:28:23.116 --> 00:28:25.660
the water especially, the farmland.

00:28:25.660 --> 00:28:28.705
As farmers, they can no
longer grow anything.

00:28:28.705 --> 00:28:32.709
He used to grow melons
and some other fruits

00:28:32.709 --> 00:28:36.755
in the farmland here, but
now he cannot grow anything.

00:28:36.755 --> 00:28:38.173
And he is really not happy about it,

00:28:38.173 --> 00:28:40.592
and he can do absolutely nothing about it.

00:28:40.592 --> 00:28:42.177
And he's complaining, basically,

00:28:42.177 --> 00:28:45.806
if the Chinese were living
in this neighborhood,

00:28:45.806 --> 00:28:48.308
then the city government

00:28:48.308 --> 00:28:51.353
and the environmental protection agency

00:28:51.353 --> 00:28:55.065
would have taken some measures
to prevent the pollution.

00:28:55.065 --> 00:28:58.610
But, now, the factory
and the city government

00:28:58.610 --> 00:29:00.111
are doing absolutely nothing,

00:29:00.111 --> 00:29:04.574
because he says the local
government officials are corrupt

00:29:04.574 --> 00:29:08.078
and were probably bought
by the cement factory.

00:29:08.078 --> 00:29:10.997
So, they can do absolutely
nothing about it,

00:29:10.997 --> 00:29:14.334
and it's really sad for them as farmers.

00:29:16.837 --> 00:29:17.671
Yeah.

00:29:18.505 --> 00:29:22.259
(speaks in foreign language)

00:29:59.254 --> 00:30:03.008
(speaks in foreign language)

00:30:18.815 --> 00:30:22.569
(speaks in foreign language)

00:30:27.324 --> 00:30:29.909
(ethnic music)

00:30:32.746 --> 00:30:34.956
- [Narrator] But couldn't the
Uyghurs reach out for help

00:30:34.956 --> 00:30:38.710
from their close Muslim
neighbors, the Pakistanis?

00:30:38.710 --> 00:30:42.464
(speaks in foreign language)

00:31:02.692 --> 00:31:03.568
(tires screech)

00:31:03.568 --> 00:31:06.446
(resounding crash)

00:31:06.446 --> 00:31:10.367
Wait a minute, Pakistan
gets favors from China?

00:31:11.326 --> 00:31:12.744
We were confused.

00:31:15.622 --> 00:31:19.709
We thought Pakistan was
supposed to be a key US ally,

00:31:19.709 --> 00:31:20.710
not China's.

00:31:25.590 --> 00:31:28.343
It's also a predominantly Muslim country.

00:31:28.343 --> 00:31:29.886
So, at the very least,

00:31:29.886 --> 00:31:31.179
wouldn't its people sympathize

00:31:31.179 --> 00:31:34.766
with the situation of
the Uyghurs in China?

00:31:39.896 --> 00:31:41.815
Just what type of a relationship

00:31:41.815 --> 00:31:44.275
does China have with Pakistan?

00:31:55.453 --> 00:31:59.124
We decided a visit to
Pakistan was in order.

00:32:06.840 --> 00:32:09.509
- There are two nations which
are fighting in the world.

00:32:09.509 --> 00:32:11.553
One is America, one is China.

00:32:11.553 --> 00:32:14.764
So, America is using
brutal way, which is war,

00:32:14.764 --> 00:32:16.307
and there is a lot of losses,

00:32:16.307 --> 00:32:20.937
and China is using a peaceful
way, and civilized way

00:32:20.937 --> 00:32:22.730
where there is no loss.

00:32:22.730 --> 00:32:24.524
- [Man] Pakistan!
(chanting)

00:32:24.524 --> 00:32:28.278
Pakistan!
(chanting)

00:32:28.278 --> 00:32:30.947
- [Crowd] Pakistan!
(shouts in foreign language)

00:32:30.947 --> 00:32:35.410
- They don't interfere,
okay, in other country.

00:32:35.410 --> 00:32:37.662
That is not like American.

00:32:37.662 --> 00:32:39.205
That is not like America

00:32:39.205 --> 00:32:41.791
who interfere in the entire world.

00:32:41.791 --> 00:32:44.377
(ethnic music)

00:32:45.837 --> 00:32:49.465
(sings in foreign language)

00:33:17.744 --> 00:33:19.078
- [Narrator] The United States

00:33:19.078 --> 00:33:23.333
is one of the largest donors
of foreign aid to Pakistan.

00:33:23.333 --> 00:33:26.628
But, most of this money is
spent on American made arms

00:33:26.628 --> 00:33:28.212
and weapon systems.

00:33:29.422 --> 00:33:32.717
The Pakistani military
justifies such spending

00:33:32.717 --> 00:33:36.429
as being necessary to defend
against the imagined threat

00:33:36.429 --> 00:33:38.389
of its archenemy, India.

00:33:40.933 --> 00:33:42.518
American aid, therefore,

00:33:42.518 --> 00:33:45.688
does little to help actual Pakistanis.

00:33:59.994 --> 00:34:02.330
Fortunately, for the Pakistanis,

00:34:02.330 --> 00:34:03.456
there are other nations

00:34:03.456 --> 00:34:05.792
that have undertaken development projects

00:34:05.792 --> 00:34:07.460
that have contributed greatly

00:34:07.460 --> 00:34:11.547
to the infrastructure and
quality of life in Pakistan.

00:34:11.547 --> 00:34:14.801
- China has been our friend
for the last 50 years.

00:34:14.801 --> 00:34:17.261
If Pakistan had any problem in the past,

00:34:17.261 --> 00:34:21.099
China came and solved
the problem of Pakistan.

00:34:22.266 --> 00:34:23.559
- [Narrator] The Karakoram Highway

00:34:23.559 --> 00:34:27.313
is the highest international
roadway in the world.

00:34:27.313 --> 00:34:31.609
It runs over 800 miles from
Kashkar, in Western China,

00:34:31.609 --> 00:34:33.528
to Islamabad, Pakistan.

00:34:35.154 --> 00:34:39.700
The KKH is a joint venture
between China and Pakistan

00:34:39.700 --> 00:34:43.871
that provides a vital link
between the two countries.

00:34:45.665 --> 00:34:48.459
A quiet graveyard just off the highway

00:34:48.459 --> 00:34:51.003
commemorates the 82 Chinese workers

00:34:51.003 --> 00:34:54.215
who lost their lives in
Pakistan during the 20 years

00:34:54.215 --> 00:34:58.219
it took to complete the
construction of the KKH.

00:35:00.638 --> 00:35:03.391
The Karakorum Highway
would not exist today

00:35:03.391 --> 00:35:05.893
were it not for the funding, hard work,

00:35:05.893 --> 00:35:08.271
and sacrifice of the Chinese.

00:35:09.981 --> 00:35:12.859
- Before the construction of KKH,

00:35:12.859 --> 00:35:16.445
the people of Kardinya
led very bored life.

00:35:17.738 --> 00:35:20.575
After the construction of KKH,

00:35:20.575 --> 00:35:23.995
we experienced different sort of changes.

00:35:25.037 --> 00:35:29.208
Culturally, economically,
socially, and politically one.

00:35:36.966 --> 00:35:38.134
- In in our area

00:35:38.134 --> 00:35:41.554
there is no industry,
only jobs, little jobs,

00:35:41.554 --> 00:35:43.890
and small homemade things.

00:35:43.890 --> 00:35:46.767
The Chinese are only one of the country

00:35:46.767 --> 00:35:50.730
who provide the which
is stuff for our people.

00:35:50.730 --> 00:35:53.816
We are six hours our border to China,

00:35:54.734 --> 00:35:56.903
so easily we are going to.

00:35:56.903 --> 00:35:58.696
- China is so near to us,

00:35:58.696 --> 00:36:02.241
so, you want to business with China.

00:36:02.241 --> 00:36:04.911
- [Narrator] In addition to
inexpensive consumer goods,

00:36:04.911 --> 00:36:08.289
Chinese technology is
also brought to Pakistan

00:36:08.289 --> 00:36:10.249
through the Karakorum.

00:36:10.249 --> 00:36:13.169
- The Chinese technology is very cheap,

00:36:13.169 --> 00:36:16.172
so the local authorities
and Pakistani government

00:36:16.172 --> 00:36:17.590
accept the abuse,

00:36:18.591 --> 00:36:23.179
and they allow them to
establish their projects.

00:36:23.179 --> 00:36:27.808
There is an agreement
between Chinese government

00:36:27.808 --> 00:36:31.646
and Pakistani government
for widening the KKH.

00:36:32.855 --> 00:36:35.232
(mumbles)

00:36:35.232 --> 00:36:37.234
As well as gas pipeline.

00:36:38.235 --> 00:36:41.656
So, the local population is very happy.

00:36:41.656 --> 00:36:43.783
They will benefit it.

00:36:43.783 --> 00:36:45.201
- [Narrator] The Chinese have also begun

00:36:45.201 --> 00:36:47.953
other mega projects in Pakistan,

00:36:47.953 --> 00:36:50.206
such as investing $200 million

00:36:50.206 --> 00:36:52.792
in the construction of Gwadar Port

00:36:52.792 --> 00:36:55.211
on the southern coast of the country.

00:36:55.211 --> 00:36:57.296
- Gwadar is considered by the Chinese

00:36:57.296 --> 00:37:01.133
as their avenue to a warm water port,

00:37:01.133 --> 00:37:03.135
a port which is
strategically close to where

00:37:03.135 --> 00:37:04.804
oil supplies go through,

00:37:04.804 --> 00:37:07.682
a port which gives them
access to the Indian Ocean

00:37:07.682 --> 00:37:09.016
and the Arabian Sea,

00:37:09.016 --> 00:37:11.811
a port that they can
use as a trade corridor,

00:37:11.811 --> 00:37:14.271
so there's the whole
idea of linking Gwadar

00:37:14.271 --> 00:37:16.482
through Belutschistan,

00:37:16.482 --> 00:37:19.110
onwards up through northern Pakistan,

00:37:19.110 --> 00:37:20.778
through the Karakorum Highway,

00:37:20.778 --> 00:37:22.321
going on through Xinjiang

00:37:22.321 --> 00:37:25.533
and onwards into Central Asia.

00:37:25.533 --> 00:37:26.492
- [Narrator] While most of these plans

00:37:26.492 --> 00:37:28.494
have yet to become reality,

00:37:28.494 --> 00:37:29.662
they reflect the ongoing

00:37:29.662 --> 00:37:32.373
and serious interest of the Chinese

00:37:32.373 --> 00:37:35.960
in maintaining close ties with Pakistan.

00:37:35.960 --> 00:37:37.378
One region of Pakistan

00:37:37.378 --> 00:37:40.172
that remains in great
need of developmental aid

00:37:40.172 --> 00:37:42.842
is the northwest frontier province

00:37:42.842 --> 00:37:45.428
in the federally
administrated tribal areas

00:37:45.428 --> 00:37:47.263
bordering Afghanistan.

00:37:51.934 --> 00:37:55.688
(speaks in foreign language)

00:37:59.358 --> 00:38:00.526
This region is infamous

00:38:00.526 --> 00:38:04.155
as a center of the Pakistani Taliban.

00:38:04.155 --> 00:38:07.867
(speaks in foreign language)

00:38:13.289 --> 00:38:14.415
The American backed effort

00:38:14.415 --> 00:38:18.460
to expel the Soviets from
Afghanistan in the 1980s

00:38:18.460 --> 00:38:22.298
provided weapons and training
to the Afghan Mujahedin.

00:38:22.298 --> 00:38:24.925
But, the needs of the
impoverished Afghan refugees

00:38:24.925 --> 00:38:26.886
who fled to neighboring Pakistan

00:38:26.886 --> 00:38:29.305
went unnoticed in Washington.

00:38:30.347 --> 00:38:33.142
(speaking in foreign language)

00:38:33.142 --> 00:38:35.644
- They start their work at
five o'clock in the morning.

00:38:35.644 --> 00:38:39.481
(speaks in foreign language)

00:38:39.481 --> 00:38:41.984
They work for eight hours a day.

00:38:41.984 --> 00:38:44.153
Do you go to school, does he?

00:38:44.153 --> 00:38:45.863
He doesn't go to school.

00:38:45.863 --> 00:38:47.489
(speaks in foreign language)

00:38:47.489 --> 00:38:49.658
He say that they don't have money

00:38:49.658 --> 00:38:51.952
to afford going to school, like,

00:38:51.952 --> 00:38:54.747
their father is very poor.

00:38:54.747 --> 00:38:56.624
All these guys look they
should go to school,

00:38:56.624 --> 00:38:58.083
but they are working with their parents.

00:38:58.083 --> 00:39:01.086
And now it's almost one
o'clock in the afternoon time,

00:39:01.086 --> 00:39:03.505
and the temperature is over 40 degrees,

00:39:03.505 --> 00:39:06.300
and they're working for their
family because they have to

00:39:06.300 --> 00:39:10.471
buy food, or buy clothes, or
other requirements of life.

00:39:16.393 --> 00:39:17.561
- [Narrator] Those who cannot afford

00:39:17.561 --> 00:39:19.980
to attend public schools

00:39:19.980 --> 00:39:23.108
find that their only
opportunity for an education

00:39:23.108 --> 00:39:25.611
lies in the Islamic madrassas.

00:39:28.447 --> 00:39:30.658
The madrassas provide a free education

00:39:30.658 --> 00:39:33.994
and books, room, and
board to the students.

00:39:33.994 --> 00:39:37.665
(sings in foreign language)

00:39:49.301 --> 00:39:52.221
Students begin by memorizing the Koran.

00:39:52.221 --> 00:39:55.265
Once they have done this,
they study other subjects,

00:39:55.265 --> 00:39:59.353
like history, logic,
philosophy, and the hadiths,

00:40:00.396 --> 00:40:03.440
or sayings and deeds of
the prophet Mohammed.

00:40:03.440 --> 00:40:07.194
(speaks in foreign language)

00:40:10.572 --> 00:40:12.533
- The government doesn't help us.

00:40:12.533 --> 00:40:13.909
The government doesn't support us.

00:40:13.909 --> 00:40:15.327
The government doesn't fund us.

00:40:15.327 --> 00:40:16.954
If the government provide us fund,

00:40:16.954 --> 00:40:19.039
then we will start engineering subjects,

00:40:19.039 --> 00:40:22.042
or science medical
subjects, or other subjects,

00:40:22.042 --> 00:40:24.169
or computer subjects.

00:40:24.169 --> 00:40:25.504
But, I'm helpless,

00:40:25.504 --> 00:40:27.756
so I have to take the
hand of someone, okay?

00:40:27.756 --> 00:40:30.676
So that he can help me and fight for me.

00:40:30.676 --> 00:40:32.970
And if you have one side
China and one side America,

00:40:32.970 --> 00:40:36.098
we will be in the favor of China.

00:40:36.098 --> 00:40:37.057
We will support China.

00:40:37.057 --> 00:40:38.225
We will work for China.

00:40:38.225 --> 00:40:41.979
(speaks in foreign language)

00:41:10.632 --> 00:41:14.178
- There was a party among
the Pakistani generals,

00:41:14.178 --> 00:41:17.347
when they were chasing glasses of wine,

00:41:17.347 --> 00:41:20.058
and they said to each other,

00:41:20.058 --> 00:41:21.768
they hoped very soon

00:41:21.768 --> 00:41:25.939
they would send American
naked ass from Afghanistan.

00:41:29.902 --> 00:41:32.237
- [Narrator] China's reputation
as a friendly neighbor

00:41:32.237 --> 00:41:35.157
does not stop at Pakistan's border.

00:41:38.911 --> 00:41:41.663
It has successfully been
out-competing the US

00:41:41.663 --> 00:41:44.666
for the favor of Afghanistan itself.

00:42:10.692 --> 00:42:13.070
After nearly 30 years of war,

00:42:13.070 --> 00:42:16.907
abandoned artillery litter
the landscape of Afghanistan

00:42:16.907 --> 00:42:20.994
like tombstones marking
the graveyard of empires.

00:42:22.079 --> 00:42:24.456
- We have enough experience with the war.

00:42:24.456 --> 00:42:26.291
We fought the Soviets.

00:42:28.877 --> 00:42:32.130
At the end, that superpower was broken.

00:42:39.721 --> 00:42:41.348
- [Narrator] Despite billions being spent

00:42:41.348 --> 00:42:43.809
on so-called aid and development,

00:42:43.809 --> 00:42:46.228
the country has become
increasingly dependent

00:42:46.228 --> 00:42:48.563
on opium production,

00:42:48.563 --> 00:42:52.109
with many blaming corruption,
and even NATO forces,

00:42:52.109 --> 00:42:55.195
for the country's
inability to move forward.

00:42:55.195 --> 00:42:59.116
- America wants to solve
everything by the gun.

00:43:00.075 --> 00:43:04.204
Gun does not bring solution,
gun increases the problems.

00:43:07.666 --> 00:43:10.836
- [Narrator] Like in Pakistan,
the Chinese have stepped in

00:43:10.836 --> 00:43:14.756
to fill the developmental void
left by the Untied States.

00:43:14.756 --> 00:43:19.678
- Right now, this reconstruction
period in Afghanistan,

00:43:19.678 --> 00:43:22.931
Chinese, they are holding
some construction company.

00:43:22.931 --> 00:43:25.809
They have built, they are busy
in some road construction.

00:43:25.809 --> 00:43:28.437
- They are not even telling our government

00:43:28.437 --> 00:43:31.273
who should be a minister,
who'd be a governor.

00:43:31.273 --> 00:43:35.610
All they are saying that
they want to see a developed

00:43:35.610 --> 00:43:38.697
and prosperous Afghanistan.

00:43:38.697 --> 00:43:41.533
- [Narrator] However,
like its Western peers,

00:43:41.533 --> 00:43:45.704
China's interest in Afghanistan
is not purely humanitarian.

00:43:47.372 --> 00:43:49.249
Rich in mineral resources,

00:43:49.249 --> 00:43:53.128
Afghanistan remains an undeveloped
source of raw materials

00:43:53.128 --> 00:43:57.007
in a world in which they
are increasingly scarce.

00:43:57.007 --> 00:44:01.094
It is Afghanistan's copper
that interest's China.

00:44:04.431 --> 00:44:07.684
The metal is used in all
aspects of modern life,

00:44:07.684 --> 00:44:11.688
including coinage, jewelry,
housing, transportation,

00:44:11.688 --> 00:44:13.857
electronics, and medicine.

00:44:16.526 --> 00:44:19.613
Afghanistan's untapped
Aynak copper deposit

00:44:19.613 --> 00:44:24.284
in Logar Province is said to
be one of the world's largest,

00:44:24.284 --> 00:44:26.703
valued at almost $90 billion.

00:44:27.746 --> 00:44:31.458
(speaks in foreign language)

00:44:50.685 --> 00:44:52.187
The China Metallurgical Group

00:44:52.187 --> 00:44:56.691
has bought a 30 year lease
for three billion dollars,

00:44:56.691 --> 00:45:00.862
the largest foreign investment
in Afghanistan's history.

00:45:03.823 --> 00:45:06.201
The royalties alone will cover almost half

00:45:06.201 --> 00:45:09.621
of the Afghan government's annual budget.

00:45:25.345 --> 00:45:29.099
(speaks in foreign language)

00:45:39.359 --> 00:45:43.530
(thunderous explosion)
(tense music)

00:45:49.995 --> 00:45:52.497
(sirens wail)

00:46:14.144 --> 00:46:15.979
On July seventh, 2008,

00:46:16.896 --> 00:46:21.067
the Indian embassy in Kabul
fell victim to a suicide bomber.

00:46:24.320 --> 00:46:27.282
Many, including the government
of the United States,

00:46:27.282 --> 00:46:30.076
believed the attack was
carried out in concert

00:46:30.076 --> 00:46:34.330
with the ISI, or Pakistani
Intelligence Service,

00:46:34.330 --> 00:46:37.167
as an act of terror against India.

00:46:39.544 --> 00:46:41.212
- When I came out from the shop,

00:46:41.212 --> 00:46:44.632
I see a lot of people was
running outside the shop.

00:46:44.632 --> 00:46:47.844
A person was injured in his head.

00:46:47.844 --> 00:46:49.596
He was full of blood.

00:46:50.597 --> 00:46:53.933
Lots of people was running
in front of the hospital,

00:46:53.933 --> 00:46:57.979
so the ambulances came,
the police and security

00:46:57.979 --> 00:47:01.775
surrounded the embassy and they
was not allowing any people.

00:47:01.775 --> 00:47:05.695
(shouting in foreign language)

00:47:22.712 --> 00:47:24.297
- [Narrator] Most of
the wounded were treated

00:47:24.297 --> 00:47:26.716
at the nearby Jamhuriat Hospital,

00:47:26.716 --> 00:47:30.553
built by China as a gift
to the Afghan people.

00:47:34.390 --> 00:47:36.392
Fortunately for Pakistan,

00:47:36.392 --> 00:47:39.354
the US decided to look the other way,

00:47:39.354 --> 00:47:42.774
and American help was nowhere to be seen.

00:47:54.118 --> 00:47:57.330
Will China show the same
level of tacit approval,

00:47:57.330 --> 00:47:59.916
or will it chide its Pakistani friends

00:47:59.916 --> 00:48:04.045
for sponsoring an unprovoked
attack against Afghanistan

00:48:04.045 --> 00:48:04.879
and India?

00:48:21.437 --> 00:48:24.274
India, home of 1.2 billion people.

00:48:26.776 --> 00:48:30.947
In 20 years, it will have a
bigger population than China.

00:48:33.992 --> 00:48:37.954
It's economy continues
to grow year after year,

00:48:37.954 --> 00:48:41.833
and it's the world's largest democracy.

00:48:41.833 --> 00:48:44.043
Could India provide a cultural

00:48:44.043 --> 00:48:47.880
and strategic counterbalance to China?

00:48:47.880 --> 00:48:49.716
- One of the main balancing forces

00:48:49.716 --> 00:48:54.512
in the emerging world of
Asia, South and East Asia,

00:48:54.512 --> 00:48:56.764
is going to be India and China,

00:48:56.764 --> 00:48:59.100
that neither is going to feel comfortable

00:48:59.100 --> 00:49:03.021
with one achieving a
position of superiority,

00:49:03.021 --> 00:49:05.898
least of all any claims to hegemony.

00:49:05.898 --> 00:49:09.402
- I would assume Asia is
a target for the Chinese.

00:49:09.402 --> 00:49:13.364
They would like to put
Asia under its control,

00:49:13.364 --> 00:49:15.950
in economic terms, in political terms,

00:49:15.950 --> 00:49:18.828
in strategic and military terms.

00:49:18.828 --> 00:49:21.372
This is where China has been active.

00:49:21.372 --> 00:49:25.376
- India is very conscious
of China and rise of China,

00:49:25.376 --> 00:49:27.295
and, also very much conscious

00:49:27.295 --> 00:49:30.840
of the difficulties India
has had with Pakistan.

00:49:30.840 --> 00:49:33.176
It is interesting to see
that China and Pakistan

00:49:33.176 --> 00:49:35.928
have shared a very important relationship

00:49:35.928 --> 00:49:37.972
over the last four decades,

00:49:37.972 --> 00:49:40.558
and, in some ways, there
is a suspicion attached

00:49:40.558 --> 00:49:42.393
in much of Indian mind

00:49:43.227 --> 00:49:45.938
as to what is the modus operandi,

00:49:45.938 --> 00:49:49.025
what are the motivations, compulsions of

00:49:49.025 --> 00:49:51.486
such a strong and close relationship,

00:49:51.486 --> 00:49:55.656
and often insinuation that
it is, perhaps, anti-India.

00:50:00.161 --> 00:50:02.330
- [Narrator] And perhaps
that is the real reason

00:50:02.330 --> 00:50:05.416
why China is so friendly to Pakistan.

00:50:09.712 --> 00:50:11.005
Beijing's influence

00:50:11.005 --> 00:50:14.675
also reaches into Delhi's
internal politics.

00:50:18.805 --> 00:50:19.806
Dharamshala,

00:50:21.599 --> 00:50:25.269
the home of the Tibetan
government in exile.

00:50:51.504 --> 00:50:55.508
After the Chinese took
control of Tibet in 1959,

00:50:55.508 --> 00:50:58.302
the Dhalai Lama and his government fled.

00:50:58.302 --> 00:51:00.888
- In 1959, when China invaded Tibet,

00:51:00.888 --> 00:51:03.140
we have very poor military.

00:51:04.433 --> 00:51:08.187
If we had a very strong
military in Tibet at that time,

00:51:08.187 --> 00:51:12.108
I think that Tibet wouldn't
have been occupied.

00:51:18.406 --> 00:51:19.907
- [Narrator] Although the US and the UN

00:51:19.907 --> 00:51:23.369
were actively trying to prevent
the spread of communism,

00:51:23.369 --> 00:51:26.289
they did not help the Tibetans.

00:51:26.289 --> 00:51:27.123
India did,

00:51:28.291 --> 00:51:31.794
and an enraged China made
them pay a bloody price,

00:51:31.794 --> 00:51:35.131
culminating in the 1962 Sino-Indian War.

00:51:36.465 --> 00:51:38.676
- After the Dhalai Lama walked into India,

00:51:38.676 --> 00:51:42.847
the overall China-Indian
relations deteriorated completely.

00:51:46.976 --> 00:51:47.810
- [Narrator] The Chinese claim

00:51:47.810 --> 00:51:49.562
that they are bringing
economic development

00:51:49.562 --> 00:51:53.899
and modernization to Tibet
and its feudal society.

00:51:53.899 --> 00:51:56.485
- China criticizes us, because China says

00:51:56.485 --> 00:51:59.739
that Tibet was feudal
country, feudal society,

00:51:59.739 --> 00:52:03.284
there was no, people were exploited.

00:52:03.284 --> 00:52:05.578
And, of course, everyone,
you know, for us, you know,

00:52:05.578 --> 00:52:09.540
we agree that Tibet was
not a perfect society.

00:52:09.540 --> 00:52:10.624
- [Narrator] But, each year,

00:52:10.624 --> 00:52:13.586
scores of Tibetans risk
disfiguring frostbite

00:52:13.586 --> 00:52:16.422
to cross the Himalayas into India.

00:52:20.134 --> 00:52:22.178
Today, refugees from Tibet,

00:52:22.178 --> 00:52:25.681
continue to find new home's in Dharamsala.

00:52:36.525 --> 00:52:39.737
So, why do so many of them come here?

00:52:39.737 --> 00:52:42.323
- My name is Lisa Young,
I am from New Zealand,

00:52:42.323 --> 00:52:45.826
and I've been volunteering
with Lha for almost two months.

00:52:45.826 --> 00:52:49.455
Lha is sort of a community college

00:52:49.455 --> 00:52:52.083
for adult Tibetan refugees

00:52:52.083 --> 00:52:56.337
and Tibetans who have just
newly arrived in India

00:52:56.337 --> 00:52:58.672
who are not eligible for
the school system here

00:52:58.672 --> 00:52:59.840
because they are too old.

00:52:59.840 --> 00:53:04.136
So, it's for refugees
from 18 to 40, mainly,

00:53:04.136 --> 00:53:08.599
and they teach free English
and Tibetan classes,

00:53:08.599 --> 00:53:11.227
French also, and computing classes,

00:53:11.227 --> 00:53:14.396
and job vocational training.

00:53:14.396 --> 00:53:16.690
And they hear about the education system

00:53:16.690 --> 00:53:19.068
that's been set up for Tibetans in India,

00:53:19.068 --> 00:53:21.112
which is separate from
the Indian school system,

00:53:21.112 --> 00:53:24.198
and that's quite often impetus for them to

00:53:24.198 --> 00:53:28.911
make the exile trek over
the Himalayas to India.

00:53:28.911 --> 00:53:31.956
That, and the two main
reasons are better education

00:53:31.956 --> 00:53:33.833
and seeing the Dhalai Lama.

00:53:33.833 --> 00:53:36.752
Because the education in
Tibet is mainly in Mandarin,

00:53:36.752 --> 00:53:39.171
and they don't get much of
a chance to speak Tibetan,

00:53:39.171 --> 00:53:42.883
and they basically have to
learn the Chinese curriculum,

00:53:42.883 --> 00:53:45.219
and a lot of them choose
not to, they don't want to,

00:53:45.219 --> 00:53:47.054
they want to learn about
Tibet and its culture.

00:53:47.054 --> 00:53:49.265
And it's definitely a
lot more preserved here,

00:53:49.265 --> 00:53:50.975
especially in Dharamsala.

00:53:50.975 --> 00:53:53.561
(ethnic music)

00:53:59.859 --> 00:54:01.151
- [Narrator] Many Tibetans feel

00:54:01.151 --> 00:54:04.613
that their ancient culture is
being systematically erased

00:54:04.613 --> 00:54:06.198
by the Han Chinese.

00:54:07.992 --> 00:54:11.620
- So these are the teachings of Buddha,

00:54:11.620 --> 00:54:13.539
and it has 108 volumes,

00:54:14.832 --> 00:54:16.417
and these are the commentaries

00:54:16.417 --> 00:54:18.502
written by the Indian masters.

00:54:18.502 --> 00:54:20.087
It has 225 volumes.

00:54:40.941 --> 00:54:44.862
So, some texts, they carry it from Tibet.

00:54:44.862 --> 00:54:48.324
It was damaged by the water, you know.

00:54:48.324 --> 00:54:49.825
- [Interviewer] How many
of these types of texts

00:54:49.825 --> 00:54:53.329
did the Chinese destroy, do you know?

00:54:53.329 --> 00:54:56.457
- I can't say the exact number.

00:54:56.457 --> 00:54:59.543
60% is destroyed by the Chinese.

00:55:00.502 --> 00:55:01.503
So, they just destroyed.

00:55:01.503 --> 00:55:05.674
They just burned and they
just threw into the water.

00:55:06.800 --> 00:55:07.760
- [Narrator] India's ability

00:55:07.760 --> 00:55:11.847
to operate independently
from Beijing is eroding.

00:55:11.847 --> 00:55:14.683
- If you were to look around Asia,

00:55:17.061 --> 00:55:21.398
China has replaced the US as
the largest trading partner

00:55:21.398 --> 00:55:25.319
for almost every country in the region.

00:55:25.319 --> 00:55:28.447
- [Narrator] India-China trade
has been growing rapidly,

00:55:28.447 --> 00:55:30.658
and a trade route has even been opened

00:55:30.658 --> 00:55:35.079
that directly connects India
and China through Tibet.

00:55:35.079 --> 00:55:39.500
- Indeed, India-China trade
has crossed in the US trade

00:55:39.500 --> 00:55:41.293
in terms of sheer numbers.

00:55:41.293 --> 00:55:42.336
- There's a growing relation,

00:55:42.336 --> 00:55:43.754
trade relation, bilateral relation,

00:55:43.754 --> 00:55:45.339
between these two country.

00:55:45.339 --> 00:55:47.966
- I think that gives Chinese certain power

00:55:47.966 --> 00:55:50.260
which people look over
their shoulder twice

00:55:50.260 --> 00:55:53.430
before they do or say something
that gets Beijing upset.

00:55:53.430 --> 00:55:56.141
- Chinese have done,
committed a lot of atrocities,

00:55:56.141 --> 00:55:57.768
and they've been allowed
to get away with it

00:55:57.768 --> 00:55:59.978
because they've been isolated for so long.

00:55:59.978 --> 00:56:01.605
There was a period in which

00:56:01.605 --> 00:56:03.065
no one knows what went on in China,

00:56:03.065 --> 00:56:04.024
and that they've opened up,

00:56:04.024 --> 00:56:06.151
they're still sort of
acting with impunity.

00:56:06.151 --> 00:56:08.070
And, because of the economic incentive,

00:56:08.070 --> 00:56:10.656
countries aren't willing to speak up.

00:56:10.656 --> 00:56:14.410
- Trade has literally
become very China driven.

00:56:14.410 --> 00:56:18.247
- India is always very
careful about the Tibet issue,

00:56:18.247 --> 00:56:21.708
and also with its relation with China.

00:56:21.708 --> 00:56:24.336
- I think it's a tightrope
that New Delhi has to walk

00:56:24.336 --> 00:56:29.133
between its increasingly
closer relations with Beijing,

00:56:29.133 --> 00:56:33.011
and also keeping Tibetan
refugees population

00:56:33.011 --> 00:56:35.305
satisfied as much as we can.

00:56:44.106 --> 00:56:45.774
- [Narrator] In March of 2008,

00:56:45.774 --> 00:56:47.985
there were protests across Tibet

00:56:47.985 --> 00:56:50.529
before the Chinese hosted the Olympics.

00:56:50.529 --> 00:56:52.447
(shouting)

00:56:52.447 --> 00:56:54.074
Many Tibetans in India

00:56:54.074 --> 00:56:58.245
decided to show their support
by marching towards Tibet.

00:57:01.165 --> 00:57:03.417
(shouting)

00:57:07.462 --> 00:57:10.382
- When we led this march, you know,

00:57:11.258 --> 00:57:14.678
we walked for nearly four months.

00:57:14.678 --> 00:57:18.432
(shouts in foreign language)

00:57:28.525 --> 00:57:30.110
Even the Kannada government,

00:57:30.110 --> 00:57:31.820
they have sent us orders saying that

00:57:31.820 --> 00:57:36.199
you can't move out of this
district, Kannada district.

00:57:36.199 --> 00:57:39.161
- India will not allow Indian territory

00:57:39.161 --> 00:57:42.372
to be used by any Tibetan protestors

00:57:42.372 --> 00:57:45.459
to undertake any political activities.

00:57:45.459 --> 00:57:47.336
- [Narrator] At Beijing's request,

00:57:47.336 --> 00:57:49.296
Delhi had its own police

00:57:49.296 --> 00:57:52.132
enforce the wishes of
the Chinese government

00:57:52.132 --> 00:57:55.052
by cracking down on the protestors.

00:57:59.556 --> 00:58:03.894
- Yeah, you know, China's
already, China is very clever,

00:58:03.894 --> 00:58:06.480
and it can use any country

00:58:06.480 --> 00:58:09.441
for their own benefit
at any point of time.

00:58:09.441 --> 00:58:11.652
(shouting)

00:58:11.652 --> 00:58:15.989
- So, when we were reaching
the district border,

00:58:15.989 --> 00:58:17.824
the Indian police stopped us.

00:58:17.824 --> 00:58:20.494
So, from our side, because
we were trained what we did,

00:58:20.494 --> 00:58:23.121
we sat down the road in the
middle of the, you know,

00:58:23.121 --> 00:58:26.792
middle of the road,
and we started praying.

00:58:26.792 --> 00:58:28.418
And some people were crying.

00:58:28.418 --> 00:58:32.798
We all got locked ourselves,
we started praying.

00:58:32.798 --> 00:58:36.718
And that made impossible
for them to get angry.

00:58:38.387 --> 00:58:40.222
And they have their own responsibility,

00:58:40.222 --> 00:58:41.348
they have their duty to perform.

00:58:41.348 --> 00:58:43.642
They have to arrest us.

00:58:43.642 --> 00:58:47.562
(shouting in foreign language)

00:59:02.619 --> 00:59:03.453
- I think perhaps

00:59:03.453 --> 00:59:05.664
I feel a bit of affinity
to the Tibetan people,

00:59:05.664 --> 00:59:07.499
'cause my parents, at least my mother,

00:59:07.499 --> 00:59:08.792
I don't know about my father,

00:59:08.792 --> 00:59:10.794
went through the cultural revolution.

00:59:10.794 --> 00:59:14.548
(shouts in foreign language)

00:59:20.387 --> 00:59:22.180
It's just weighing on me a little bit,

00:59:22.180 --> 00:59:24.599
because everyone things
I'm Tibetan when I'm here,

00:59:24.599 --> 00:59:25.434
which is lovely,

00:59:25.434 --> 00:59:28.145
'cause I've really grown
to love the Tibetan people,

00:59:28.145 --> 00:59:29.271
but, before I came her,

00:59:29.271 --> 00:59:31.690
I was warned by a lot
of local Indian people,

00:59:31.690 --> 00:59:33.692
and also tourists that have been here,

00:59:33.692 --> 00:59:35.026
when I told them that I was Chinese,

00:59:35.026 --> 00:59:37.279
they were really surprised.

00:59:46.121 --> 00:59:49.124
Some people were actually
saying quite extreme things,

00:59:49.124 --> 00:59:51.460
that people might think
I was a spy from China,

00:59:51.460 --> 00:59:54.421
and that people would
react negatively here.

00:59:54.421 --> 00:59:57.132
They would get angry with me.

00:59:57.132 --> 00:59:59.342
Not angry, then they
would be staring at me,

00:59:59.342 --> 01:00:01.970
and they would make my stay
here very uncomfortable.

01:00:01.970 --> 01:00:05.724
(shouts in foreign language)

01:00:09.269 --> 01:00:10.103
I had to decide

01:00:10.103 --> 01:00:12.105
whether I was gonna tell
people here that I was Chinese,

01:00:12.105 --> 01:00:15.400
and, unfortunately I decided not to.

01:00:15.400 --> 01:00:19.154
(shouts in foreign language)

01:00:22.365 --> 01:00:24.034
And I think that was a mistake,

01:00:24.034 --> 01:00:27.120
because I think they
would've accepted me fine.

01:00:27.120 --> 01:00:29.748
They've got friends in
Tibet that are Chinese,

01:00:29.748 --> 01:00:32.500
and they are very open and
welcoming of Chinese people

01:00:32.500 --> 01:00:34.377
because that's what the
Dhalai Lama teaches them,

01:00:34.377 --> 01:00:36.004
to show compassion to everyone,

01:00:36.004 --> 01:00:38.465
your enemies and your friends.

01:00:41.426 --> 01:00:43.386
- [Narrator] India's not the only country

01:00:43.386 --> 01:00:45.805
where China tries to control Tibetans

01:00:45.805 --> 01:00:48.475
outside of its national borders.

01:00:50.268 --> 01:00:53.396
(ethnic music)

01:00:53.396 --> 01:00:56.775
Nepal is home to 28 million people.

01:00:56.775 --> 01:01:00.946
It is sandwiched between
two giants, India and China.

01:01:03.990 --> 01:01:06.576
India has always had a
significant influence

01:01:06.576 --> 01:01:10.747
on the culture of Nepal,
it's economics, and trade.

01:01:14.417 --> 01:01:16.503
But China has become increasingly active

01:01:16.503 --> 01:01:18.838
in the politics of Nepal,

01:01:18.838 --> 01:01:20.799
with much Chinese attention placed

01:01:20.799 --> 01:01:24.803
on the 20,000 Tibetan
refugees who reside there.

01:01:26.805 --> 01:01:28.640
- The key word is predominant,

01:01:28.640 --> 01:01:31.351
vis-a-vis China's relations with Nepal.

01:01:31.351 --> 01:01:33.770
I think what the Tibetans are doing here,

01:01:33.770 --> 01:01:36.523
what the Americans are
doing here vis-a-vis Tibet

01:01:36.523 --> 01:01:39.526
is of utmost concern to the Chinese.

01:01:41.569 --> 01:01:44.030
- [Narrator] Tibetan refugees
began coming to Nepal

01:01:44.030 --> 01:01:47.200
after the Chinese occupation of Tibet.

01:01:49.619 --> 01:01:53.790
The Jawalakhel camp in Kathmandu
is home to 1,000 refugees.

01:01:57.085 --> 01:01:59.754
And about 500 are employed there,

01:01:59.754 --> 01:02:02.090
manufacturing woven carpets.

01:02:04.342 --> 01:02:07.011
The government of Nepal
is wary of being seen

01:02:07.011 --> 01:02:10.348
as helping the Tibetan refugees too much.

01:02:10.348 --> 01:02:11.975
- To counterbalance our overwhelming

01:02:11.975 --> 01:02:15.562
political and economic
dependence on India,

01:02:16.771 --> 01:02:20.942
we try to lean over backwards
to be nice to China.

01:02:22.360 --> 01:02:26.531
It's pretty clear that
the Tibetan protests,

01:02:26.531 --> 01:02:28.616
the Chinese don't like it.

01:02:28.616 --> 01:02:31.703
They are extremely sensitive to this,

01:02:32.662 --> 01:02:35.415
and that sensitivity is very easily

01:02:35.415 --> 01:02:37.667
brought to bear on the Nepal government.

01:02:37.667 --> 01:02:40.753
So, if the Chinese are
going to be angry about

01:02:40.753 --> 01:02:42.714
Tibetan's running around in Nepal,

01:02:42.714 --> 01:02:45.133
we are willing to give
that a sympathetic ear

01:02:45.133 --> 01:02:47.260
and crack down on Tibetans here,

01:02:47.260 --> 01:02:49.429
as long as China is happy.

01:02:50.972 --> 01:02:52.432
- [Narrator] The Nepali
government's treatment

01:02:52.432 --> 01:02:55.310
of Tibetan protestors is clearly different

01:02:55.310 --> 01:02:58.646
than its treatment of Nepali protestors.

01:03:02.233 --> 01:03:06.446
Police ignore burning effigies
and tires and blocking roads,

01:03:06.446 --> 01:03:09.115
as long as it's done by Nepalis.

01:03:19.125 --> 01:03:22.086
Although the treatment of
Tibetan refugees in Nepal

01:03:22.086 --> 01:03:24.172
may seem similar on the surface

01:03:24.172 --> 01:03:26.216
to their treatment in India,

01:03:26.216 --> 01:03:29.594
the mechanism behind it is far different.

01:03:29.594 --> 01:03:32.055
(guns fire)

01:03:32.055 --> 01:03:36.226
For 10 years, a bloody
civil war raged across Nepal

01:03:37.143 --> 01:03:40.521
as Maoist rebels took
up arms against the king

01:03:40.521 --> 01:03:43.775
and the Maoists gained popular support.

01:03:45.276 --> 01:03:49.072
After the king was forced
out of power in 2008,

01:03:49.072 --> 01:03:53.201
the Maoists were elected
to run the new government.

01:03:54.577 --> 01:03:58.748
The party's name is a clear
tribute to China's Chairman Mao.

01:03:59.999 --> 01:04:03.753
(speaks in foreign language)

01:04:16.849 --> 01:04:19.185
(guns fire)

01:04:21.104 --> 01:04:22.522
During the civil war,

01:04:22.522 --> 01:04:26.234
sherpas camping in the remote
snowy passes of the Himalaya

01:04:26.234 --> 01:04:30.405
reported seeing caravans
of ponies loaded with guns

01:04:30.405 --> 01:04:34.575
crossing from China into Nepal
during the dead of night.

01:04:45.044 --> 01:04:49.382
- Our party's policy,
the international policy,

01:04:49.382 --> 01:04:51.634
is equal distance relation.

01:04:54.679 --> 01:04:58.850
Not more close to the India,
not more close to China.

01:04:59.892 --> 01:05:02.270
- [Narrator] India has historically
been the major influence

01:05:02.270 --> 01:05:04.272
on life in Nepal,

01:05:04.272 --> 01:05:07.525
so, in practice, a
policy of equal distance

01:05:07.525 --> 01:05:10.653
will require Nepal to
realign its interests

01:05:10.653 --> 01:05:12.655
more closely to China's.

01:05:16.576 --> 01:05:20.246
While the Maoists claim to have
brought democracy to Nepal,

01:05:20.246 --> 01:05:23.499
in reality, their behavior is consistent

01:05:23.499 --> 01:05:25.793
with that of their namesake.

01:05:25.793 --> 01:05:28.296
(tense music)

01:05:46.272 --> 01:05:49.901
Maoists stormed the
offices of the Nepali Times

01:05:49.901 --> 01:05:53.529
and physically assaulted
Kunda Dixit and his staff

01:05:53.529 --> 01:05:56.449
in an attempt to silence the press.

01:06:00.453 --> 01:06:04.040
China was able to benefit
from the Maoist's willingness

01:06:04.040 --> 01:06:07.960
to destroy the freedoms
of expression in Nepal.

01:06:08.878 --> 01:06:11.172
In response to pressure from China,

01:06:11.172 --> 01:06:15.301
Nepal agreed to ban all
anti-China activity on its soil.

01:06:24.352 --> 01:06:28.022
China is bringing Nepal within its orbit,

01:06:28.022 --> 01:06:29.774
but what happens now?

01:06:30.983 --> 01:06:33.528
Once China controls a territory,

01:06:33.528 --> 01:06:36.113
what's in store for its future?

01:06:36.989 --> 01:06:39.575
Let's take a look at Hong Kong.

01:06:40.910 --> 01:06:43.829
(orchestral music)

01:06:54.173 --> 01:06:58.344
Hong Kong is one of the
world's most developed cities.

01:07:06.352 --> 01:07:07.687
An icon of Asia.

01:07:11.190 --> 01:07:13.025
The pearl of the East.

01:07:25.329 --> 01:07:27.707
Hong Kong has also long been at the center

01:07:27.707 --> 01:07:29.959
of imperial disputes.

01:07:29.959 --> 01:07:33.337
It was taken by the British
Empire from the Qing Dynasty

01:07:33.337 --> 01:07:36.215
after the First Opium War.

01:07:36.215 --> 01:07:39.218
(speaks in Chinese)

01:07:58.738 --> 01:08:00.531
After reunification,

01:08:00.531 --> 01:08:03.284
the Chinese promised
to preserve Hong Kong's

01:08:03.284 --> 01:08:06.328
highly successful laissez faire economy

01:08:06.328 --> 01:08:09.874
and its political autonomy, rule of law,

01:08:09.874 --> 01:08:12.710
and western style civil liberties

01:08:12.710 --> 01:08:14.879
under a paradigm that would be dubbed

01:08:14.879 --> 01:08:16.964
one country, two systems.

01:08:18.924 --> 01:08:21.677
This is why Hong Kong is so crucial.

01:08:21.677 --> 01:08:25.514
It is a litmus test
for Chinese intentions.

01:08:25.514 --> 01:08:26.974
When China gains control

01:08:26.974 --> 01:08:31.145
over an economy or political
system, what happens?

01:08:32.146 --> 01:08:36.609
Can China be trusted to
respect that system's autonomy?

01:08:36.609 --> 01:08:39.904
Or will China try to dominate it?

01:08:39.904 --> 01:08:42.031
And, unlike other parts of China,

01:08:42.031 --> 01:08:43.407
perhaps the best test

01:08:43.407 --> 01:08:46.410
is not how ethnic minorities are treated,

01:08:46.410 --> 01:08:50.581
but, rather, religious
minorities, like the Falun Gong.

01:08:52.792 --> 01:08:56.545
- If you bump into one
Hong Kongese on the street,

01:08:56.545 --> 01:09:01.133
or ask some kind of human
rights activities in Hong Kong,

01:09:01.133 --> 01:09:03.385
what is the most sensitive task

01:09:03.385 --> 01:09:07.556
of one country, two systems
is Falun Gong issue.

01:09:07.556 --> 01:09:08.599
- [Narrator] The Falun Gong

01:09:08.599 --> 01:09:11.310
is a modern Chinese spiritual practice

01:09:11.310 --> 01:09:14.146
that was founded in China in 1992.

01:09:15.231 --> 01:09:18.400
- This is a spiritual practice

01:09:18.400 --> 01:09:22.571
that has deep roots in school
of Taoism or the Buddhism.

01:09:23.781 --> 01:09:27.409
Our main principles are three words.

01:09:27.409 --> 01:09:29.537
Truthfulness, compassion, tolerance.

01:09:29.537 --> 01:09:31.205
And we believe that's the principle

01:09:31.205 --> 01:09:34.500
that the entire universe operates under.

01:09:35.834 --> 01:09:37.461
- [Narrator] It's explosive popularity

01:09:37.461 --> 01:09:40.756
scared the Chinese communist party.

01:09:40.756 --> 01:09:44.176
On the 20th of July, 1999, it was banned,

01:09:45.678 --> 01:09:47.721
and the brutal campaign of persecution

01:09:47.721 --> 01:09:49.557
began in the mainland.

01:10:02.027 --> 01:10:03.571
Falun Gong practitioners

01:10:03.571 --> 01:10:06.323
sought refuge all over the world,

01:10:06.323 --> 01:10:10.494
including Taiwan, Japan,
the US, and even Hong Kong.

01:10:12.788 --> 01:10:16.709
Compared to China, Hong Kong
remained an island of tolerance

01:10:16.709 --> 01:10:18.294
for the Falun Gong.

01:10:20.963 --> 01:10:25.426
Even today, as busloads of
tourists from the mainland

01:10:25.426 --> 01:10:27.428
come to visit Hong Kong

01:10:27.428 --> 01:10:30.681
and take in the view from Victoria Peak,

01:10:30.681 --> 01:10:33.392
Folun Gong practitioners are free,

01:10:33.392 --> 01:10:36.061
under Hong Kong's constitution,

01:10:36.061 --> 01:10:41.025
to peacefully demonstrate
in support of their beliefs,

01:10:41.025 --> 01:10:44.528
including displays about
human rights violations

01:10:44.528 --> 01:10:46.697
by the Chinese government.

01:10:50.284 --> 01:10:52.119
On the surface it would appear

01:10:52.119 --> 01:10:55.539
that one country, two systems is working.

01:10:57.041 --> 01:10:57.875
Or is it?

01:10:58.917 --> 01:11:02.463
- One of the issues raised
when you introduce Hong Kong

01:11:02.463 --> 01:11:05.299
is whether or not the Chinese idea

01:11:06.175 --> 01:11:09.553
of one country, two systems is stable.

01:11:09.553 --> 01:11:11.013
I don't think so.

01:11:11.013 --> 01:11:12.598
- [Narrator] Under Beijing's pressure,

01:11:12.598 --> 01:11:13.724
the Hong Kong government

01:11:13.724 --> 01:11:16.894
routinely violated its own constitution

01:11:16.894 --> 01:11:19.938
by refusing entry to
Falun Gong practitioners

01:11:19.938 --> 01:11:22.316
who try to visit the territory.

01:11:22.316 --> 01:11:25.152
- Every country have immigration control.

01:11:25.152 --> 01:11:28.238
They are entitled to
refuse someone, no problem.

01:11:28.238 --> 01:11:32.076
But, racial and religious discrimination

01:11:32.076 --> 01:11:36.038
cannot be a reason of
refusing people's enter.

01:11:36.038 --> 01:11:39.792
So, when we talk about
one country, two systems,

01:11:39.792 --> 01:11:44.296
it's like, you know,
gradually really disappearing.

01:11:44.296 --> 01:11:46.215
- [Narrator] Is one country, two systems

01:11:46.215 --> 01:11:49.802
starting to become one
country, one system?

01:11:51.512 --> 01:11:54.515
(speaks in Chinese)

01:12:08.278 --> 01:12:09.822
- [Narrator] Theresa Chu herself

01:12:09.822 --> 01:12:12.825
was deported when she attempted to visit.

01:12:12.825 --> 01:12:15.452
- Chinese leader Wu Jing
Hao was visiting there.

01:12:15.452 --> 01:12:19.748
We had 1,000 Taiwan
Falun Gong practitioner,

01:12:19.748 --> 01:12:23.919
from six year old kid to
80-something aged old lady,

01:12:26.922 --> 01:12:31.093
were violently repatriated
from Hong Kong to Taiwan.

01:12:33.095 --> 01:12:34.888
They used some kind of blanket,

01:12:34.888 --> 01:12:38.475
wrap me from here until
up around my knees.

01:12:41.103 --> 01:12:45.691
In detain room, we have
no water, no refreshment,

01:12:45.691 --> 01:12:47.109
no place to rest.

01:13:00.122 --> 01:13:03.292
So, you can see, how hostile they are.

01:13:04.251 --> 01:13:06.295
It's not like a free society.

01:13:06.295 --> 01:13:09.172
It's not like a pearl of the East.

01:13:09.172 --> 01:13:10.424
Why?

01:13:10.424 --> 01:13:13.510
Because of black hand, the invisible hand

01:13:13.510 --> 01:13:16.471
behind Hong Kong sovereign government

01:13:16.471 --> 01:13:18.181
the Chinese reaching.

01:13:18.181 --> 01:13:21.184
(speaks in Chinese)

01:13:39.202 --> 01:13:41.622
(rock music)

01:14:39.221 --> 01:14:42.349
- [Narrator] After being defeated
by the Chinese communists,

01:14:42.349 --> 01:14:46.520
the KMT, or Chinese Nationalists,
led by Chiang Kai-shek

01:14:47.479 --> 01:14:49.523
fled to the island of Taiwan

01:14:49.523 --> 01:14:51.650
and designated Taipei

01:14:51.650 --> 01:14:55.654
as the capital of the
Republic of China in 1949.

01:14:57.155 --> 01:14:59.157
The KMT ruled the island

01:14:59.157 --> 01:15:02.577
under an oppressive authoritarian regime,

01:15:03.954 --> 01:15:07.457
but it was successful in
creating rapid economic growth

01:15:07.457 --> 01:15:08.959
that has made Taiwan

01:15:08.959 --> 01:15:13.130
one of the most industrialized
countries in the world.

01:15:14.881 --> 01:15:17.926
Eventually, the KMT's iron grip

01:15:17.926 --> 01:15:20.971
gave way to a democratic system in Taiwan,

01:15:20.971 --> 01:15:23.807
creating the first true
ethnic Chinese democracy

01:15:23.807 --> 01:15:25.559
in world history.

01:15:25.559 --> 01:15:27.978
(rock music)

01:15:40.490 --> 01:15:44.160
(sings in foreign language)

01:15:51.251 --> 01:15:55.171
- Most important thing for each citizen

01:15:55.171 --> 01:15:56.798
is to be independent.

01:15:56.798 --> 01:15:58.508
I mean, yourself.

01:15:58.508 --> 01:16:02.679
So, you have to independent
and the country be independent.

01:16:03.847 --> 01:16:05.932
So, I think that's the
most important thing,

01:16:05.932 --> 01:16:09.311
and I'm not that kind of
nationalist independent guy,

01:16:09.311 --> 01:16:11.855
but I want an independent country

01:16:11.855 --> 01:16:13.732
with all the independent citizens.

01:16:13.732 --> 01:16:15.650
Think independently,

01:16:15.650 --> 01:16:17.611
and do independently,

01:16:17.611 --> 01:16:19.905
and vote independently.

01:16:19.905 --> 01:16:23.033
Try to think everything independently,

01:16:23.033 --> 01:16:25.493
don't believe in media.

01:16:25.493 --> 01:16:28.330
So, I think the citizens should be smarter

01:16:28.330 --> 01:16:32.083
and should try to control the politicians,

01:16:32.083 --> 01:16:35.295
try to use the politicians as the tools

01:16:35.295 --> 01:16:37.213
to achieve your ideals.

01:16:50.935 --> 01:16:52.604
- [Narrator] An authoritarian regime

01:16:52.604 --> 01:16:57.150
and rapid economic growth
leading to Chinese democracy.

01:16:57.150 --> 01:17:01.279
Could Taiwan be a model for
the future of mainland China?

01:17:01.279 --> 01:17:03.698
- If democracy exists,

01:17:03.698 --> 01:17:07.869
and is established, more
strengthened in the region,

01:17:09.079 --> 01:17:10.997
I believe it's not just,

01:17:10.997 --> 01:17:13.875
it would not just benefit
the people in Taiwan,

01:17:13.875 --> 01:17:17.504
but also benefit surrounding
countries, especially China.

01:17:17.504 --> 01:17:19.381
- The youngsters on the mainland,

01:17:19.381 --> 01:17:23.510
they are gradually changing
their worldview, you know,

01:17:24.719 --> 01:17:27.889
they are not that inward looking anymore,

01:17:27.889 --> 01:17:32.644
but they can see by themselves
what's going on in Taiwan,

01:17:32.644 --> 01:17:36.564
especially in Taiwan's
democratic developments.

01:17:38.983 --> 01:17:41.986
(speaks in Chinese)

01:17:50.161 --> 01:17:50.995
In the long run,

01:17:50.995 --> 01:17:55.166
we can change the very nature
of the Chinese communism.

01:17:56.835 --> 01:17:59.421
And hoping that someday
that mainland China

01:17:59.421 --> 01:18:04.134
can be converted into a
free and democratic society.

01:18:04.134 --> 01:18:08.304
- We believe that China is
moving to a right direction

01:18:09.556 --> 01:18:12.392
that develops the economy

01:18:12.392 --> 01:18:16.062
and improve the quality
of life of everyone,

01:18:17.230 --> 01:18:21.401
and, at the same time promote
democracy and equality.

01:18:28.032 --> 01:18:30.368
- [Narrator] As the
Chinese economy has grown,

01:18:30.368 --> 01:18:31.911
a process of normalization

01:18:31.911 --> 01:18:36.166
between Taiwan and the mainland has begun.

01:18:36.166 --> 01:18:39.335
(speaking in Chinese)

01:18:43.339 --> 01:18:45.592
(cheering)

01:18:50.972 --> 01:18:54.684
- I hope that the
mainland and Taiwan could

01:18:54.684 --> 01:18:57.770
come together to work out a better system,

01:18:57.770 --> 01:19:00.190
and, also, be more connected.

01:19:01.858 --> 01:19:04.986
- [Narrator] Investment,
trade, and political exchange

01:19:04.986 --> 01:19:06.946
have grown at a rapid pace.

01:19:06.946 --> 01:19:10.033
- This a very critical moment for us

01:19:10.033 --> 01:19:13.453
to develop a healthy and better relations

01:19:14.913 --> 01:19:16.748
with Chinese mainland.

01:19:18.541 --> 01:19:21.461
- [Narrator] But, is this
ultimately good for Taiwan?

01:19:21.461 --> 01:19:24.047
Or, does economic integration with China

01:19:24.047 --> 01:19:27.800
pose a threat to Taiwanese democracy?

01:19:27.800 --> 01:19:30.803
(speaks in Chinese)

01:19:51.950 --> 01:19:55.703
- They try to create this image
that, at least symbolically,

01:19:55.703 --> 01:19:57.413
that they are a peaceful country,

01:19:57.413 --> 01:19:59.123
they are rising peacefully,

01:19:59.123 --> 01:20:03.294
and they wish to deliver this
sense of sincere to the world

01:20:04.712 --> 01:20:08.591
that we are rising
economically and politically,

01:20:08.591 --> 01:20:12.470
but, in a way that world
stability will be maintained.

01:20:12.470 --> 01:20:14.347
- We need to accept that China

01:20:14.347 --> 01:20:17.600
become really big power in the world,

01:20:17.600 --> 01:20:21.354
but the problem is what
kind of China we want

01:20:22.230 --> 01:20:25.066
in the future, in the 21st century.

01:20:25.066 --> 01:20:29.153
Some people are talking
about that China may

01:20:29.153 --> 01:20:31.739
replace the United States in the future.

01:20:31.739 --> 01:20:35.368
But, if this China is also current China,

01:20:35.368 --> 01:20:38.121
I don't think it's really a
very good thing for the world,

01:20:38.121 --> 01:20:39.122
for the humanity.

01:20:39.122 --> 01:20:42.583
- Being a big country,
being a big, strong country,

01:20:42.583 --> 01:20:46.212
the United States of America should mount

01:20:46.212 --> 01:20:48.047
pressure on the Chinese government.

01:20:48.047 --> 01:20:49.882
- If the West really wanted
to speak up, it would,

01:20:49.882 --> 01:20:50.967
but it chooses not to

01:20:50.967 --> 01:20:52.802
because our products come from China,

01:20:52.802 --> 01:20:54.429
we rely on China's economy.

01:20:54.429 --> 01:20:56.389
- We never ask ourselves
what to we do, however,

01:20:56.389 --> 01:20:57.807
if they get really so rich

01:20:57.807 --> 01:20:59.642
that they're richer than we are.

01:20:59.642 --> 01:21:03.229
And that we are making ourselves
utterly dependent on them.

01:21:03.229 --> 01:21:06.315
- The world is relying on
China a lot at the moment,

01:21:06.315 --> 01:21:09.444
and it's too afraid to
really speak up for Tibet

01:21:09.444 --> 01:21:11.320
or for any of the other issues.

01:21:11.320 --> 01:21:12.989
- I believe that the
international community

01:21:12.989 --> 01:21:16.451
should continue to talk about
the human rights problems,

01:21:16.451 --> 01:21:17.827
the democracy in China.

01:21:17.827 --> 01:21:20.371
If not, I believe we are just helping

01:21:20.371 --> 01:21:23.124
to create a new empire,

01:21:23.124 --> 01:21:27.253
and I believe it's not good,
really for the 21st century.

01:21:32.967 --> 01:21:35.386
(rock music)

01:21:38.306 --> 01:21:42.059
(sings in foreign language)

